        "original_id": "6ad74448-e093-5ccc-b368-b0e7017f9b8e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Pueraria, Pleiospilos, Pueraria montana\n- Places: Asia, South Africa\n- Concepts: plant genera, species relationships, common names, hybrids\n\nFacts:\n- Pueraria is a genus of 15–20 plant species native to Asia.\n- Pleiospilos is a genus of succulent flowering plants in the Aizoaceae family that is native to South Africa.\n- Pueraria montana is closely related to the Pueraria species P. edulis and P. phaseoloides.\n- The common name kudzu is used for Pueraria montana, P. edulis, P. phaseoloides, and hybrids between them.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
